OL,3,GNEWSAWrong cat may have been buried
OL,4,Aafter mix-up at vets
OL,5,
OL,6,FA woman may have been given the wrong
OL,7,Fcat to bury due to a mix-up at the vets
OL,8,Fafter it was run over.
OL,10,FZoe Downs, from Seaham in County
OL,11,FDurham, who had been feeding the stray
OL,12,Fanimal for two years, took it to Seaham
OL,13,FVets and requested the body be returned
OL,14,Fto her if an owner could not be found.
OL,16,FBut, after she had buried the animal,
OL,17,Fthe vets called to say she may have
OL,18,Fbeen given the wrong cat, which she
OL,19,Fsaid left her "heartbroken".
OL,23,APub: 13-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,399,390,260,160,0,100
